      "description": "Coverage.py measures code coverage, typically during test execution. It uses\nthe code analysis tools and tracing hooks provided in the Python standard\nlibrary to determine which lines are executable, and which have been executed.\n\nCoverage.py runs on Pythons 2.3 through 3.2.\n\nDocumentation is at `nedbatchelder.com <http://nedbatchelder.com/code/coverage/3.4b1>`_.  Code repository and issue\ntracker are at `bitbucket.org <http://bitbucket.org/ned/coveragepy>`_.\n\nNew in 3.2: Branch coverage!\n\nNew in 3.3: .coveragerc files.\n\nNew in 3.4: Better control over source to measure.",
